{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "prop:diffuse-att",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For every \\(\\vartheta_n=(L_n,D_n)\\in\\Theta_n\\) under the balanced rank-one one-block L-mask assumptions and every deterministic \\(A_n\\) satisfying treated support, normalization, nonnegativity, and diffuseness, \\[\\Pr_{\\mathbb P_{\\vartheta,n},\\Xi_n,\\Zeta_n}\\{\\tau_{A,n}\\in\\mathrm{CI}_{A,n}\\}\\ge1-\\alpha.\\] The half-length is at most \\(a_n\\widehat R_{\\alpha/2,n}+z_{1-\\alpha/4}\\sigma\\lVert A_n\\rVert_F\\); this is a coverage result from nuclear--operator duality, not an optimal-length assertion.",
