    "justification": "Nuclear/operator duality transfers the global counterfactual certificate to a pre-specified diffuse ATT, while the independent treated-cell noise is covered separately.",
    "gap": "Functional-specific papers derive sharper tailored laws; this result is solely a coverage-valid duality corollary.",
    "consumer": "Applied staggered-adoption studies can reuse the global matrix uncertainty set for one valid weighted ATT interval.",
    "proof_tex": "Because \\(P_{W_n}A_n=A_n\\) and \\(Y_n=L_n+D_n+E_n\\),\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\widehat\\tau_{A,n}-\\tau_{A,n}\n&=\\langle A_n,P_{W_n}(Y_n-\\widehat L_n)\\rangle\n-\\langle A_n,D_n\\rangle\\\\\n&=\\langle A_n,P_{W_n}(L_n-\\widehat L_n)\\rangle\n+\\langle A_n,P_{W_n}E_n\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nNuclear--operator duality gives\n\\[\n|\\langle A_n,P_{W_n}(L_n-\\widehat L_n)\\rangle|\n\\le\\lVert A_n\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}}\n\\lVert P_{W_n}(\\widehat L_n-L_n)\\rVert_*.\n\\]\nApply Lemma \\ref{lem:balanced-wsvd-certificate} with miscoverage level \\(\\alpha/2\\), which is admissible because \\(0<\\alpha/2<1/4\\). Its honesty event\n\\[\n\\mathcal E_L=\n\\{\\lVert P_{W_n}(\\widehat L_n-L_n)\\rVert_*\n\\le\\widehat R_{\\alpha/2,n}\\}\n\\]\nhas probability at least \\(1-\\alpha/2\\). Assumption \\ref{ass:gaussian-cells} makes the cell errors on \\(W_n\\) independent of the observed coordinates on \\(\\Omega_n\\), and\n\\[\n\\langle A_n,P_{W_n}E_n\\rangle\n\\sim\\mathcal N(0,\\sigma^2\\lVert A_n\\rVert_F^2).\n\\]\nTherefore the two-sided Gaussian event\n\\[\n\\mathcal E_E=\n\\{|\\langle A_n,P_{W_n}E_n\\rangle|\n\\le z_{1-\\alpha/4}\\sigma\\lVert A_n\\rVert_F\\}\n\\]\nhas probability \\(1-\\alpha/2\\). A union bound gives\n\\(\\Pr(\\mathcal E_L\\cap\\mathcal E_E)\\ge1-\\alpha\\). On this intersection, the two preceding inequalities are exactly the membership inequality \\(\\tau_{A,n}\\in\\mathrm{CI}_{A,n}\\). Finally, Assumption \\ref{ass:att-diffuse} gives \\(\\lVert A_n\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}}\\le a_n\\), hence the asserted half-length bound. Treated support is used in the algebra; normalization and nonnegativity give the ATT interpretation but are not needed for the coverage inequality. No optimal-length conclusion is drawn.",
